  "live_records": {
    "q-94857": {
      "dom_id": "step-q94857",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X∼N(1.8,{\\sigma }^{2})$ and $P(X\\ge 4)=0.2119,$ find ${\\sigma }^{2},$ rounded to $2$ decimal places.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.7\\,$ | $\\,0.7580\\,$ | $\\,0.7611\\,$ | $\\,0.7642\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.8\\,$ | $\\,0.7881\\,$ | $\\,0.7910\\,$ | $\\,0.7939\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.9\\,$ | $\\,0.8159\\,$ | $\\,0.8186\\,$ | $\\,0.8212\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "First, we convert the given probability into a cumulative probability using the complement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 4) & =1-P(X\\ge 4) \\\\  & =1-0.2119 \\\\  & =0.7881\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 4) & =0.7881 \\\\ P(Z\\le \\frac{4-1.8}{\\sigma }) & =0.7881 \\\\ Φ(\\frac{2.2}{\\sigma }) & =0.7881 \\\\ \\frac{2.2}{\\sigma } & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.7881)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(0.80)=0.7881\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(0.7881)=0.80.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2.2}{\\sigma } & =0.80 \\\\ \\sigma  & =\\frac{2.2}{0.80} \\\\ \\sigma  & =2.75.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2}={2.75}^{2}=7.56\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nto $2$ decimal places.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
