    "q-342032": {
      "dom_id": "step-q342032",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X∼N(0,{\\sigma }^{2})$ is a normal random variable with $P(|X|<2)=0.6826,$ find ${\\sigma }^{2}.$ \n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,1.0\\,$ | $\\,0.8413\\,$ | $\\,0.8438\\,$ | $\\,0.8461\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.1\\,$ | $\\,0.8643\\,$ | $\\,0.8665\\,$ | $\\,0.8686\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.2\\,$ | $\\,0.8849\\,$ | $\\,0.8869\\,$ | $\\,0.8888\\,$ |\n\n${\\sigma }^{2}=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "First, we express the given probability as\n\n$$\nP(|X|<2)=P(-2<X<2).\n$$\n\nThen, we find the cumulative probability using symmetry:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-2<X<2) & =0.6826 \\\\ 2P(0<X<2) & =0.6826 \\\\ P(0<X<2) & =0.3413 \\\\ P(X<2)-P(X<0) & =0.3413 \\\\ P(X<2)-0.5 & =0.3413 \\\\ P(X<2) & =0.8413 \\\\ P(X\\le 2) & =0.8413\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 2) & =0.8413 \\\\ P(Z\\le \\frac{2-0}{\\sigma }) & =0.8413 \\\\ Φ(\\frac{2}{\\sigma }) & =0.8413 \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sigma } & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.8413)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(1.00)=0.8413\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(0.8413)=1.00.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sigma } & =1 \\\\ \\sigma  & =\\frac{2}{1} \\\\ \\sigma  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =(2)^{2}=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
