    "q-342059": {
      "dom_id": "step-q342059",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X∼N(3,{\\sigma }^{2})$ is a normal random variable with $P(1<X<5)=0.3758,$ use the table to find  $\\sigma ,$ rounded to $2$ decimal places.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ | $\\,0.08\\,$ | $\\,0.09\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.4\\,$ | $\\,0.6808\\,$ | $\\,0.6844\\,$ | $\\,0.6879\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.5\\,$ | $\\,0.7157\\,$ | $\\,0.7190\\,$ | $\\,0.7224\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.6\\,$ | $\\,0.7486\\,$ | $\\,0.7517\\,$ | $\\,0.7549\\,$ |\n\n*Hint: Note that the interval $1<X<5$ is symmetric about the mean $\\mu =3.$*\n\n$\\sigma ≈$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "First, note that the given interval is symmetric about the mean:\n\n$$\nP(1<X<5)=P(3-2<X<3+2)\n$$\n\nSo, we find the cumulative probability using symmetry:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1<X<5) & =0.3758 \\\\ 2P(3<X<5) & =0.3758 \\\\ P(3<X<5) & =0.1879 \\\\ P(X<5)-P(X<3) & =0.1879 \\\\ P(X<5)-0.5 & =0.1879 \\\\ P(X<5) & =0.6879 \\\\ P(X\\le 5) & =0.6879\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 5) & =0.6879 \\\\ P(Z\\le \\frac{5-3}{\\sigma }) & =0.6879 \\\\ Φ(\\frac{2}{\\sigma }) & =0.6879 \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sigma } & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.6879)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(0.49)=0.6879\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(0.6879)=0.49.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sigma } & =0.49 \\\\ \\sigma  & =\\frac{2}{0.49} \\\\ \\sigma  & ≈4.08\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
